{"license":"DANS Licence","fileAccessRequest":false,"metadataBlocks":{"citation":{"displayName":"Citation Metadata","name":"citation","fields":[{"typeName":"title","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Erfgoed van de Oorlog, Bystander Memories, interview RG-50.570.0010"},{"typeName":"otherId","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"otherIdAgency":{"typeName":"otherIdAgency","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"DANS-KNAW"},"otherIdValue":{"typeName":"otherIdValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"easy-dataset:41681"}}]},{"typeName":"author","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"authorName":{"typeName":"authorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Vrije Universiteit"}},{"authorName":{"typeName":"authorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"United States Holocaust Memorial Museum"}}]},{"typeName":"datasetContact","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"datasetContactName":{"typeName":"datasetContactName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"D.G.  Hondius"},"datasetContactAffiliation":{"typeName":"datasetContactAffiliation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam"}}]},{"typeName":"dsDescription","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"dsDescriptionValue":{"typeName":"dsDescriptionValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"<p>De geïnterviewde werd op 7 februari 1914 geboren in Leiden. Gedurende de oorlog was hij politieagent.  In deze functie is hij betrokken geweest bij het ophalen van een joods gezin in Den Haag.  Hij is eveneens aanwezig geweest bij de deportatie van joden uit Barneveld naar kamp Westerbork. Dit waren joden die aanvankelijk vrijgesteld waren van deportatie vanwege hun functie in de maatschappij. Hij gaat uitvoerig op deze gebeurtenissen in en gaat in op de gevoelens die hij hierbij had. Naast deze gebeurtenissen heeft de geïnterviewde in de meidagen gevochten nabij Katwijk. Hier verhaalt hij eveneens gedetailleerd over.<br><br>The interviewee was born on 7 February, 1914 in Leiden. During the war he was a policeman.  In this function he was involved in the deportation of a Jewish family in The Hague. He was also present during the deportation from Jews from Camp Barneveld to Camp Westerbork. The Jews in Barneveld were a group who were at first exempt from deportation because of their position in society. He talks extensively about these events and about his feelings about all of this. In addition to these events he fought in the first days of the occupation in May 1940, near Katwijk. He also gives details about this.<\/p>"}},{"dsDescriptionValue":{"typeName":"dsDescriptionValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Date Submitted: 2010-04-01"}},{"dsDescriptionValue":{"typeName":"dsDescriptionValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"<p>Van dit interview zijn eveneens uitgebreide samenvattingen met tijd-codes beschikbaar in zowel het Nederlands als Engels. Zie de Inleiding voor een snel overzicht van de gehele collectie en de contactgegevens. Er zijn tevens verschillende bestanden bijgevoegd betreffende het project en dit specifieke interview.<br><br><br>Besides the transcript there is an extensive summary available of the interview in both Dutch and English with time-codes inserted. See the Introduction for a quick overview of the entire collection and the contact details. There are also several documents and reports available concerning the project and this particular interview.<\/p>"}}]},{"typeName":"subject","multiple":true,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":["Arts and Humanities"]},{"typeName":"keyword","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Leiden"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Den Haag"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Vlissingen"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Barneveld"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Westerbork"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"leger"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"militair"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"politie"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"arrestatie"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Joden"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Katwijk"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Den Helder"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"marine"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Nederlands-Indië"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"mobilisatie"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"zelfmoord"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"kranten"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Het Volk"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Grebbeberg"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"gevechten"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"parachutisten"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"capitulatie"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"koningin Wilhelmina"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Cleveringa"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Sicherheitsdienst"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Rauter"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Fischer"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"fietsen"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Grüne Polizei"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Amersfoort"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Theresienstadt"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"The Hague"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"army"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"militairy"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"policeman"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"arresting Jews"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"deportations"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Jews"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"persecution"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"marines"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Dutch East Indies"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"mobilisation"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"suicide"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"newspapers"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"fights"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"parachutists"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"capitulation"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"queen Wilhelmina"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"bicycles"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"oral history"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Tweede Wereldoorlog"}}]},{"typeName":"language","multiple":true,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":["Dutch"]},{"typeName":"productionDate","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"2004-12-18"},{"typeName":"contributor","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"contributorName":{"typeName":"contributorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"dr. Dienke Hondius, Vrije Universiteit, adviseur"}},{"contributorName":{"typeName":"contributorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"drs. Anna Timmerman, coördinator in Nederland, onderzoeker"}},{"contributorName":{"typeName":"contributorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Nathan Beyrak, United States Holocaust Memorial Museum, Project Director; Christian Url, Oral History Department"}},{"contributorName":{"typeName":"contributorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Interakt: Rene Mendel productie; Martijn van Haalen interview; Paul Enkelaar en Bernd Wouthuysen, camera"}},{"contributorName":{"typeName":"contributorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"drs. Machlien Vlasblom, Vrije Universiteit, onderzoeksassistent"}}]},{"typeName":"distributionDate","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"2010-03-28"},{"typeName":"dateOfDeposit","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"2004-12-18"},{"typeName":"series","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"seriesInformation":{"typeName":"seriesInformation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"<p>Bystander Memories bevat in totaal 59 interviews met Nederlandse niet-joodse ooggetuigen van de jodenvervolging. Deze interviews vormen een onderdeel van een project uitgevoerd door het United States Holocaust Memorial Museum, Oral History Department, waar het valt onder de 'Europe Interview Projects: Interviews with Witnesses, Collaborators, and Perpetrators'. Naast de Nederlandse interviews zijn er ook interviews gemaakt in het (Wit)Russisch, Grieks, Macedonisch, Pools, Oekraiens, Servisch, Ests, Lets, Litouws, Moldavisch, Frans, Duits, Roemeens. De aantallen interviews per land variëren sterk. Het project is in 1996 begonnen en loopt nog steeds, zie website USHMM: http:\/\/www.ushmm.org\/research\/collections\/oralhistory\/<br><br>Since 1996, United States Holocaust memorial Museum's (USHMM) Department of Oral History has conducted a documentation project to collect the testimonies of individuals who were not direct victims of the Holocaust. These interviews are with witnesses, collaborators, and perpetrators. In ten years, over 600 interviews have been conducted in the following European countries: Czech Republic, Estonia, France, Germany, Latvia, Lithuania, Moldova, The Netherlands, Poland, Romania, the Ukraine, Bosnia-Herzegovina, and Serbia. These interviews serve not only as corroboration of what Jewish victims and survivors report in their interviews and memoirs, they also create a broader understanding of the tragic events of World War II by adding the perspectives of non-Jewish populations. The Dutch interviews are accessible at DANS for scientific research only.<\/p>"}}]}]},"dansRights":{"displayName":"Rights Metadata","name":"dansRights","fields":[{"typeName":"dansRightsHolder","multiple":true,"typeClass":"primitive","value":["Unknown"]},{"typeName":"dansPersonalDataPresent","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"Unknown"},{"typeName":"dansMetadataLanguage","multiple":true,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":["Dutch","English"]}]},"dansRelationMetadata":{"displayName":"Relation Metadata","name":"dansRelationMetadata","fields":[{"typeName":"dansAudience","multiple":true,"typeClass":"primitive","value":["https:\/\/www.narcis.nl\/classification\/D34300"],"expandedvalue":[{"@id":"https:\/\/www.narcis.nl\/classification\/D34300","termName":[{"lang":"nl","value":"Moderne en contemporaine geschiedenis"},{"lang":"en","value":"Modern and contemporary history"}],"vocabularyUri":"https:\/\/www.narcis.nl\/classification\/"}]},{"typeName":"dansCollection","multiple":true,"typeClass":"primitive","value":["https:\/\/vocabularies.dans.knaw.nl\/collections\/ssh\/660537e4-b005-43da-9dc3-207dabbc0a08","https:\/\/vocabularies.dans.knaw.nl\/collections\/ssh\/ce21b6fb-4283-4194-9369-b3ff4c3d76e7","https:\/\/vocabularies.dans.knaw.nl\/collections\/ssh\/213a59ea-8d36-42c6-b30b-474ebbdef61d","https:\/\/vocabularies.dans.knaw.nl\/collections\/ssh\/cfa04ed6-4cd0-4651-80cb-ed4ca8fa14f3"],"expandedvalue":[{"@id":"https:\/\/vocabularies.dans.knaw.nl\/collections\/ssh\/660537e4-b005-43da-9dc3-207dabbc0a08","vocabularyUri":"https:\/\/vocabularies.dans.knaw.nl\/collections"},{"@id":"https:\/\/vocabularies.dans.knaw.nl\/collections\/ssh\/ce21b6fb-4283-4194-9369-b3ff4c3d76e7","vocabularyUri":"https:\/\/vocabularies.dans.knaw.nl\/collections"},{"@id":"https:\/\/vocabularies.dans.knaw.nl\/collections\/ssh\/213a59ea-8d36-42c6-b30b-474ebbdef61d","vocabularyUri":"https:\/\/vocabularies.dans.knaw.nl\/collections"},{"@id":"https:\/\/vocabularies.dans.knaw.nl\/collections\/ssh\/cfa04ed6-4cd0-4651-80cb-ed4ca8fa14f3","vocabularyUri":"https:\/\/vocabularies.dans.knaw.nl\/collections"}]},{"typeName":"dansRelation","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"dansRelationType":{"typeName":"dansRelationType","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"relation"},"dansRelationText":{"typeName":"dansRelationText","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Anna Timmerman, Machteloos? Ooggetuigen van de Jodenvervolging (Amsterdam 2007)"}}]}]},"dansTemporalSpatial":{"displayName":"Temporal and Spatial Coverage","name":"dansTemporalSpatial","fields":[{"typeName":"dansTemporalCoverage","multiple":true,"typeClass":"primitive","value":["1930 - 1946"]},{"typeName":"dansSpatialCoverageText","multiple":true,"typeClass":"primitive","value":["Leiden, Den Haag, Barneveld, Katwijk"]}]},"dansDataVaultMetadata":{"displayName":"Data Vault Metadata","name":"dansDataVaultMetadata","fields":[{"typeName":"dansDataversePid","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"doi:10.17026\/DANS-25H-G6SC"},{"typeName":"dansDataversePidVersion","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"2.2"},{"typeName":"dansBagId","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"urn:uuid:a69c2aab-5700-478a-93ec-3dd626a745b7"},{"typeName":"dansNbn","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"urn:nbn:nl:ui:13-88m-d5q"}]}}}